-- title:
--   Lower bound d for components of closed fibres
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $R$ a domain that is a finitely generated $k$-algebra, and $C$ a domain that is a finitely generated $R$-algebra, with $C$ also a $k$-algebra compatibly with the map $k \to R \to C$. Suppose given $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and elements $z_0,\dots,z_{d-1} \in C$ (a map $z \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to C$) that are algebraically independent over $R$, together with a nonzero $r \in R$ such that every $c \in C$ satisfies: for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, the element $r^n \cdot c$ is integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[z_0,\dots,z_{d-1}]$ generated by the range of $z$. Let $p$ be a maximal ideal of $R$ with $r \notin p$, and let $Q$ be a prime of $C$ that is minimal among the primes containing the image ideal $p\,C = p \cdot C$ generated by the image of $p$ under $R \to C$ (i.e. $Q$ lies in the minimal primes of `p.map (algebraMap R C)`). Then $d \le \operatorname{ringKrullDim}(C/Q)$, the inequality being read in $\mathbb{N}_\infty \cup \{\bot\}$ after coercing $d$.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of the lower bound for the dimension of the irreducible components of the closed fibres of a dominant morphism: over the locus where $r$ is invertible, $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ is, up to integrality, an affine space of relative dimension $d$, and every component of a closed fibre has dimension at least $d$. The proof invokes the dimension formula $\operatorname{ht} P + \dim(A/P) = \dim A$ for affine domains over a field, and the result is used in [`Ideal.exists_ne_zero_and_forall_isMaximal_radical_map_isPrime`](thm.html#Ideal.exists_ne_zero_and_forall_isMaximal_radical_map_isPrime).
